&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining the Real Estate and Workplace Operations (REWO) team within DoorDash’s Finance Organization. We design, build, and operate inclusive, inspiring, and functional spaces that help employees do their best work, removing physical friction so teams can focus on what matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior leadership role overseeing the Workplace and Facilities team in India. You will drive efficient, employee-focused operations across multiple locations, combining operational expertise, strategic planning, vendor management, and facilities leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop an insourced and outsourced Workplace and Facilities team across multiple locations, maintaining consistency in operations, service delivery, and employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set team objectives aligned with organizational goals; define clear performance metrics and hold the team accountable to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and implement processes, playbooks, and initiatives that align with global workplace strategies and drive operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage space planning and allocation to accommodate evolving organizational needs, balancing functionality, employee experience, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee office events to ensure they reflect company culture and deliver engaging, impactful experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all facilities meet local regulations, safety standards, and company policies; partner with cross-functional teams to stay ahead of changing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Global Operations Center on crisis scenarios (natural disasters, evacuations, pandemics) and ensure the team executes business continuity plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor and contractor relationships for food, beverages, and essential services including contract administration, renewals, RFPs, and ongoing service level assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Real Estate on lease renewals, new builds, and renovations to ensure smooth day-one operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use occupancy data, employee surveys, and spend analysis to develop workplace strategies and identify opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the annual operating budget, including financial variance tracking and cost-saving initiatives that maintain service quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead change management for workplace initiatives, communicating clearly and consistently with stakeholders throughout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular updates to senior leadership on operations, project progress, and KPIs; maintain strong relationships with executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build collaborative relationships with cross-functional partners, landlords, vendors, and contractors across time zones and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Sustainability Team to identify and implement environmental improvements across office locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 5+ years of Workplace leadership experience managing teams across multiple countries and organizational levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven ability to mentor and develop team members, build cross-functional partnerships, and drive a high-performance culture. Comfortable setting goals, pivoting quickly, and managing multiple priorities simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills; able to present clearly to all levels, including senior executives. Strong interpersonal skills and a relationship-first approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organization &amp;amp; Execution: &lt;/strong&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented; thrives in fast-paced environments and ensures nothing falls through the cracks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving: &lt;/strong&gt;Proactive and solutions-oriented, with sound judgment and the ability to anticipate needs and act independently when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience managing infrastructure service providers (custodial, catering, maintenance, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage complex, cross-functional projects from planning through completion, including office construction and renovation logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Proficient in budget development, financial planning, and procurement/sourcing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology: &lt;/strong&gt;Hands-on with Google Suite, Jira, Coupa, Slack, Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, and Sigma. Strong Excel and Google Sheets skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility: &lt;/strong&gt;Able to work in-office 5 days a week, travel ~10%, and work overnight shifts (Monday–Friday).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Knowledge: &lt;/strong&gt;Familiarity with workplace trends (hybrid/remote work, workplace design) and their impact on collaboration and productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About DoorDash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DoorDash, our mission to empower local economies shapes how our team members move quickly, learn, and reiterate in order to make impactful decisions that display empathy for our range of users—from Dashers to merchant partners to consumers. We are a technology and logistics company that started by enabling door-to-door delivery, and we are looking for team members who can help us go from a company that is known as the place you order food to a company that people turn to for any and all goods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;DoorDash is growing rapidly and changing constantly, which gives our team members the opportunity to share their unique perspectives, solve new challenges, and own their careers. We&#39;re committed to supporting employees’ happiness, healthiness, and overall well-being by providing comprehensive benefits and perks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you need any accommodations, please inform your recruiting contact upon initial connection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
